NAME
       expr - evaluate an expression

SYNOPSIS
       expr EXPRESSION

DESCRIPTION
       Evaluate and print. Operators, lowest precedence first:
       |   &   = != < <= > >=   + -   * / %   :   match substr
       index length + ( ) Comparisons are numeric when both
       sides are integers, else byte strings. STRING : REGEX
       matches a basic regular expression anchored at the
       start. Exit status: 0 result neither empty nor 0, 1 it
       is, 2 invalid expression, 3 other error. Integers are
       64-bit; overflow is an error.

NOTES
       Integers are 64-bit: a result beyond that prints
       "result too large" and exits 2 (GNU expr uses arbitrary
       precision).

SEE ALSO
       sh(1)

